Edge match (dcsvr_edge_match, round and rounded-rectangle focus shapes; ported from GitHub PR #26): inside the fade band
the composition crossfades the full-detail focus view with a periphery of 3-6x fewer pixels per degree, which reads as a
ring. With it the focus view's detail first tapers to the periphery's own resolution (a tent blur whose width grows from
0 to one periphery texel over the first dcsvr_edge_match share of the band, sized from the screen-space derivatives of
both views), then fades. Band pixels only; 0 (the default) leaves the shader's output unchanged.
The constant goes before focusViewShape (offset 16; focusViewShape moves to 20, the layout stays 96 bytes), in
ProjectionPS.hlsl and in the copy Far depth keeps (ProjectionPS.nofardepth.hlsl), so that focusViewShape stays last in
that copy's cbuffer, where Far depth's constants are injected (tests/depthwarp checks that injection).
The two-layer output pass (dcsvr_twolayer_ps.hlsl) has no edge match: the compositor enlarges the periphery there.
